meta {
  name: CreateProject
  type: grpc
  seq: 3
}

grpc {
  url: {{coreGrpc}}
  method: /dop.v1.HierarchyService/CreateProject
  body: grpc
  auth: none
}

metadata {
  x-actor-id: {{actorId}}
  x-account-id: {{accountId}}
  x-request-id: {{$guid}}
}

body:grpc {
  [
    {
      "workspace": { "id": "{{workspaceId}}" },
      "name": "Cockpit",
      "description": "An example project",
      "idempotency_key": "{{$guid}}"
    }
  ]
}

docs {
  Who is calling and in which account go in the METADATA, never in the body
  (ADR-0017, convention 5).

  The creation is lean on purpose: repositories, resources and the link to the
  board come in through `UpdateProject`. The account is NOT given — it is
  inherited from the workspace, and letting the caller give it would open the way
  for a project to be born in an account that is not its workspace's.
}
